{
  "note": "What each valid case of users.json means to the engine's user index: the UserFilter (crates/auth-front/src/console/filter.rs) the console layer translates it into, as JSON, with relative times resolved against `now` (rounded to the minute in the engine). A day is the whole day: created:2026-10-01 is that day, > after it, <= until its end; an instant (RFC 3339, now, -7d) is a point. A claim value is a JSON scalar when it reads as one, text otherwise. Read only by the Rust test.",
  "now": "2026-10-12T10:30:00Z",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "empty",
      "text": "",
      "filter": {}
    },
    {
      "name": "one-word",
      "text": "ada",
      "filter": {
        "words": [
          {
            "value": "ada"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "negated-word",
      "text": "-ada",
      "filter": {
        "words": [
          {
            "negated": true,
            "value": "ada"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "quoted-phrase",
